@@ -221,3 +221,13 @@ The equivalent HTTP interface is `http://127.0.0.1:8766` with a local bearer tok
 from the configured `ONSHAPE_NATIVE_RUNTIME/bridge.json`. The companion owns the
 HTTP listener; the extension executes browser-session commands. Prefer MCP in
 both clients. Never expose pairing tokens, cookies or private model data in logs.
+
+### H2 literal source variables (experimental paired writer)
+
+Compile and validate the source locally first. The writer accepts literal ASSIGNED/LENGTH variables in source order; it does not allocate feature IDs. For each variable, use official Browser control to open the normal Variable editor in the exact configured test studio. Leave one fresh unnamed LENGTH draft with zero length. Discover controls from current DOM, never sample IDs or guessed coordinates.
+
+Run `h2cad experimental-populate-variable SOURCE --logical-id '#length'` with the exact target, `--bridge-config`, `--tab-id`, and pinned `--journal` arguments. For each subsequent source variable, supply every preceding observed operation in order with repeated `--previous-variable-op-id OP_ID`. Results record logical-to-native identities. The writer rejects named drafts, wrong mode/type, changed source, changed preceding or unrelated tree, and unresolved writes. Native parameter identities/defaults and both source quantity expressions are retained.
+
+A candidate receipt or Save invocation is not completion. Require independent exact saved-idle readback and an observed journal operation before allocating the next variable. If pending, inspect the exact target with Browser and complete only through normal controls when available; then run `experimental-reconcile-saved-source-variable OP_ID` with the same pinned config/journal and exact current tab. If a fresh same-target tab is needed to observe saved state, do not replay the write or alter the original pending draft. Reconciliation is read-only and retains the barrier on mismatch.
+
+Record normal UI error presentation separately. `regeneration_verified: false` is deliberate: definition readback does not prove dependent expression evaluation. Later dependent planes/sketches must establish it. This is Browser plus CLI skill orchestration, not autonomous standalone allocation. H2 has no REST write fallback.
